To use:

1. copy feeder-stats.pl & diablo-stats.sh (or cyclone-stats.sh if you are
   running Cyclone) to your bin directory
2. edit diablo-stats.sh (or cyclone-stats.sh) to match your site requirements
3. check that feeder-stats.pl '#!/path/perl' points to your copy of Perl5
4. if you want graphs (PNG-format) you'll need the Chart and GD perl modules:
   http://www.perl.com/CPAN/modules/by-module/GD/
   http://www.perl.com/CPAN/modules/by-module/Chart/
   (or get them at the nearest CPAN mirror)
5. copy the feeder-stats.conf to your /news directory
6. copy the logo.gif file to your $HtmlDir directory or put your own
   (not too big) logo.gif there.
7. install a crontab job to run diablo-stats.sh (or cyclone-stats.sh):
   ie.  59 * * * * /usr/local/bin/diablo-stats.sh > /dev/null 2>&1

Grouping by label (Diablo log files only):

   Add -L to the feeder-stats.pl command line in diablo-stats.sh to report
   incoming and outgoing feeds per dnewsfeeds label instead of per host
   name.  This helps when peers have no PTR record (the tables then show
   bare IP addresses) or feed from several addresses.  The label of an
   incoming host is taken from the inhost, host and hostname lines of
   dnewsfeeds and from diablo.hosts, including wildcards and CIDR ranges
   (read from the directory given with -C).  A host that matches no label
   is reported under its own name, as before; alias: lines in
   feeder-stats.conf still apply to such hosts.  Outgoing feeds use the
   label in the name of the queue file.  Run 'sh test-label.sh' in this
   directory to check the option on made-up log lines.

